<section class="section walkthrough-approach">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="walkthrough-story">
      <div>
        <h2>There is a lot to learn. You do not have to learn it alone.</h2>
        <p>A dealer walkthrough can move quickly. By the time you leave, you may have seen dozens of switches, valves, and connections without feeling ready to use them. I have been there myself.</p>
        <p>My personalized walkthrough gives those pieces a sensible order. Before we meet, I research your RV and prepare a printed guide for us to follow together. During our visit, we work through the systems, connect them to everyday camping tasks, and leave room for your questions and hands-on practice.</p>
        <p><strong>Your walkthrough price includes every topic listed below that applies to your RV.</strong> You do not need to choose topics from a menu or pay separately for each one. I guide us through the applicable topics in an organized sequence, with time for your questions and hands-on practice.</p>
        <p><strong>The list is long because your RV does a lot.</strong> It is my preparation roadmap, not a test for you. You are not expected to memorize it or arrive knowing the terminology. We focus on the equipment you actually have, skip what does not apply, and spend more time where you need it.</p>
        <p>Whether this is your first RV or your third, the goal is the same: understand this RV and feel more comfortable using it.</p>
      </div>
      <img src="/assets/images/walkthru.png" alt="Professor Jerry explaining an RV system during a personalized walkthrough" width="600" height="400">
    </div>
    <div class="walkthrough-benefits">
      <article><span class="eyebrow">Before we meet</span><h3>Prepared for your RV</h3><p>I research your year, make, model, floorplan, and equipment so our time together has a clear direction.</p></article>
      <article><span class="eyebrow">During your visit</span><h3>Follow along and try it</h3><p>Your printed guide gives you a place to follow the discussion, take notes, and flag questions as we go.</p></article>
      <article><span class="eyebrow">Afterward</span><h3>Something to return to</h3><p>Keep your printed guide and notes, plus one complimentary hour of follow-up, onsite consulting. With the optional video package, your entire walkthrough is recorded and organized into individually labeled how-to clips on a USB drive, ready whenever you need a refresher.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
